--- PAYMENT MOCKUP FLOW (critical for demo) ---

Goal: Clicking "Place Order" must always result in a success screen,
with a believable loading state in between.

Step-by-step:

  1. User fills checkout form (contact, shipping, fake card fields)

  2. On "Place Order" click (checkout.js):
     - Validate required fields client-side
     - Hide form, show full-screen processing overlay
     - Overlay shows: spinner + "Processing your payment..." text
     - After 1500ms timeout, submit a hidden form via JS to POST /payments/process/

  3. POST /payments/process/ (payments/views.py):
     - Read cart from session
     - Create Order + OrderItems in DB with status = "confirmed"
     - Clear cart session
     - Redirect to /orders/confirmation/<order_id>/

  4. Confirmation page shows:
     - Green checkmark animation (CSS only)
     - Order number
     - Itemized summary
     - Estimated delivery (hardcoded: 3-5 business days for demo)
     - "Continue Shopping" CTA → /

Fake card fields (checkout Step 3):
  - Card number input (no Luhn validation — any 16-digit string passes)
  - Expiry (MM/YY format, any future date passes)
  - CVV (any 3-digit string passes)
  - Name on card (any non-empty string passes)
  - These fields are never sent to the backend — purely cosmetic for demo


--- CHECKOUT STEPS (JS-driven, single page) ---

All three steps live in checkout.html.
JavaScript shows/hides step sections by toggling a .hidden class.
No page reload between steps.

  Step 1 — Contact & Shipping
    - Email field (or auto-filled if logged in)
    - Full name, address, city, province, ZIP, country (dropdown: PH default)
    - "Continue to Shipping" button

  Step 2 — Shipping Method
    - 3 hardcoded options (Standard 3-5 days free, Express 1-2 days ₱150,
      Same-day Metro only ₱300)
    - Radio buttons, selection updates order summary total
    - "Continue to Payment" button

  Step 3 — Payment
    - Fake card fields (described above)
    - Order summary always visible (sticky sidebar on desktop)
    - "Place Order" button → triggers mock payment flow

Step indicator at the top: 1 → 2 → 3 with active/completed states via CSS classes.


